{"id":"SMA-453","title":"Bump testcontainers to drop vulnerable tokio-tar (GHSA-j5gw-2vrg-8fgx)","description":"Dependabot alert #5 (high): `tokio-tar <= 0.3.1` is vulnerable to PAX header desynchronization ([GHSA-j5gw-2vrg-8fgx](<https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j5gw-2vrg-8fgx>), RUSTSEC-2025-0110 "Tarmageddon"). No patched `tokio-tar` release exists — the fix lives in the maintained `astral-tokio-tar` fork (>= 0.5.6).

`tokio-tar 0.3.1` enters `rs/Cargo.lock` via `testcontainers 0.24` / `testcontainers-modules 0.12` (dev-dependencies of `paigasus-iam`). Newer testcontainers releases depend on the patched `astral-tokio-tar` instead.

**Fix**: bump to `testcontainers 0.27` + `testcontainers-modules 0.15` in `paigasus-iam`, verify `tokio-tar` leaves the lockfile, and confirm the roundtrip tests still pass. Dependabot won't do this itself because there is no patched version of `tokio-tar` proper.","priority":{"value":0,"name":"No priority"},"url":"https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-453/bump-testcontainers-to-drop-vulnerable-tokio-tar-ghsa-j5gw-2vrg-8fgx","gitBranchName":"feature/sma-453-bump-testcontainers-to-drop-vulnerable-tokio-tar-ghsa-j5gw","createdAt":"2026-07-05T18:51:25.520Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-05T18:51:25.520Z","archivedAt":null,"completedAt":null,"startedAt":"2026-07-05T18:51:25.557Z","canceledAt":null,"dueDate":null,"slaStartedAt":null,"slaMediumRiskAt":null,"slaHighRiskAt":null,"slaBreachesAt":null,"slaType":"all","status":"In Progress","statusType":"started","labels":["Improvement"],"attachments":[],"documents":[],"createdBy":"Sven Maschek","createdById":"ba6021cb-56c5-43aa-9797-fab3599d7ead","assignee":"Sven Maschek","assigneeId":"ba6021cb-56c5-43aa-9797-fab3599d7ead","team":"Sven Maschek","teamId":"7178572e-d61f-4cf0-bbcb-4e03c8d9f39e"}

